hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18101","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Saeed ibn Abi Ayyub and Haywah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Busr ibn Saeed, from Khalid ibn Adi al-Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever receives a kindness from his brother without asking and without his self aspiring to it, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is only provision that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has driven to him."
"24229","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, that Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj informed him, that Busr ibn Sa'id informed him, from Khalid ibn Adi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever is brought a kindness from his brother, without looking forward to it and without asking, let him accept it and not return it, for it is only provision which Allah has driven to him."
